  "title": "Darwix Commercial Lending Handbook - 2026",
  "content": "Darwix Commercial Lending Handbook - 2026\nSection 1: General Business Loan Eligibility Thresholds\nThis policy outlines the official underwriting thresholds for all commercial credit facilities.\n1. Minimum Operating History: The borrowing business must have at least 6 months of verifiable operating history for\nshort-term working capital loans, and a minimum of 12 to 24 months for prime commercial term loans.\n2. Minimum Gross Revenue: Businesses must demonstrate minimum average monthly gross revenues of ,000 (,000\nannualized), verified via 3 to 6 months of official business checking bank statements.\n3. Geographic Eligibility: The borrower entity must be registered and actively operating within any of the 50 United\nStates or the District of Columbia. Foreign entities are strictly ineligible.",
